  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(8x)}+6)=$",
  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${x}^{5}\u226b\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(8x)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(8x)}=\\infty \n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(8x)}+6)=\\infty \n$$",
